# Generated, not authored. Asset catalogs are written by Xcode and a tool cache
# is rewritten on every run, so formatting them either fights a generator or
# produces a diff that reappears.
**/*.xcassets/
**/.impeccable/

# Overspecified the same way. OpenSpec writes its commands and skills when it is
# initialised, and the repositioning documents are vendored verbatim: the point
# of vendoring them is that they stay byte-identical to the pack, which the
# format check would quietly undo.
.opencode/
docs/repositioning/

# And once more, for the negative fixture. It is invalid Vue on purpose: the
# adapter has to report a component its parser rejects, and a parser that
# prettier had already fixed would be a test of nothing. Prettier cannot parse
# it, and an unparseable file aborts the whole format check rather than warning
# about one file.
packages/source-vue/fixtures/vue-broken/

# And once more, for the OpenSpec artifacts, archived and live. Prettier has no
# stable fixed point on a long requirement or task line with continuation lines:
# writing the file leaves it in a shape the next check still reports, so the gate
# flips between two answers. These are checked by `openspec validate` instead,
# which is the check that actually knows what their shape has to be.
openspec/changes/
openspec/specs/

# The same, for the native build. Gradle writes its CMake cache into the app's
# tree, and the app-level .gitignore covers that path, but prettier does not read
# .gitignore: without this line, anyone who has built Android locally fails the
# format check on files no one wrote.
**/android/app/.cxx/

# And once more, for watchman. It drops a short-lived cookie into a directory
# while it scans it, so the format check can list a file that is already gone by
# the time prettier reads it, and the commit fails on that race rather than on a
# format. The repository's .gitignore keeps the cookies out of a diff, but
# prettier does not read .gitignore, so it needs the line. The commit that added
# this failed its own gate on exactly that file.
**/.watchman-cookie-*
